          %p
            Generally, a
            %em theta function
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
            \-function,
            = succeed "-function)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+section"} holomorphic section
            of a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarized+variety"}> principally polarizing
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+line+bundle"} holomorphic line bundle
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+torus"} complex torus
            \/
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+variety"} abelian variety
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Polishchuk03"} Polishchuk 03, section 17
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobian+variety"} Jacobian variety
            (
            %a{:href => "#Beauville"}> Beauville
            ) such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundles"} prequantum line bundles
            for (abelian)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            = succeed "-function" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theta+characteristics"} Theta characteristics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{z}
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^g
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+torus"} complex torus
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^g/\mathbb{Z}^g
            = succeed "-function" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi z
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{z} \mapsto \theta(\mathbf{z})
            satisfying certain transformation properties, and this is how theta functions are considered.
          %p
            Those theta functions encoding sections of line bundles on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobian+variety"} Jacobian variety
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J(\Sigma)
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant+line+bundles"}> determinant line bundles
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Freed87"} Freed 87, pages 30-31
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
            modulus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\tau}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            and are hence really functions also of this variable
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi z
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi z
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{z},\mathbf{\tau}) \mapsto \theta(\mathbf{z}, \mathbf{\tau})
            with certain transformation properties. These are the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+theta+functions"} Riemann theta functions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hitchin+connection"} Hitchin connection
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+Riemann+surfaces"} moduli space of Riemann surfaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_\Sigma
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hitchin90"}> Hitchin 90, remark 4.12
            ). In the special case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is complex 1-dimensional of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus"} genus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g = 1
            (hence a complex
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo ,
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo ,
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (z,\tau) \mapsto \theta(z,\tau)
            of two variables with the pertinent transformation properties is a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+theta+function"} Jacobi theta function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            but also on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
            these are properly called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+forms"} Jacobi forms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobian+varieties"} Jacobian varieties
            have non-abelian generalizations to line bundles on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks+of+vector+bundles"} moduli stacks of vector bundles
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
            higher than one, whose sections may then be thought of as
            %em generalized theta functions
            (
            %a{:href => "#BeauvilleLaszlo93"}> Beauville-Laszlo 93
            ).
          %p
            Specifically in the context of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+theory"} number theory
            = succeed "," do
