          %h3#IdeaInQuantization In quantization
          %p
            Theta functions are naturally thought of as being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+states+%28in+geometric+quantization%29"} states
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            of the given complex space, the given holomorphic line bundle being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundle"} prequantum line bundle
            and the condition of holomorphicity of the section being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization"} polarization
            condition. See for instance (
            %a{:href => "#Tyurin02"}> Tyurin 02
            ). In this context they play a proming role specifically in the quantization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} higher dimensional Chern-Simons theory
            and of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual higher gauge theory
          %p
            Specifically the fact that in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+Chern-Simons+theory"} quantization of Chern-Simons theory
            in the abelian case, and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographically
            dual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+functions"} partition functions
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            the choice of polarization is induced from the choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\tau}
            on a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            and for each such choice there is then a section/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
            depending on a coordinate
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{z}
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobian"} Jacobian
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J(\Sigma)
            is reflected in the double coordinate dependence of the theta function:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi z
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi θ
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi gauge
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi field
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi configuration
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi on
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Σ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi complex
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi structure
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi on
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\theta(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{\tau})
                  \=
                  \\theta\left(gauge\;field\;configuration\;on\;\Sigma\;, \; complex\;structure\;on\;\Sigma\right)
                  \\,.
          %p
            See (
            %a{:href => "#AlvaresGaumeMooreVafa86"}> AlvaresGaumé-Moore-Vafa 86, p. 4
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Freed87"} Freed 87, section 4
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FalcetoGawedzki94"} Falceto-Gawedzki 94
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BunkeOlbrich94"} Bunke-Olbrich 94, around def. 4.5
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GelcaUribe10a"} Gelca-Uribe 10a
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GelcaUribe10b"} Gelca-Uribe 10b
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GelcaHamilton12"} Gelca-Hamilton 12
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GelcaHamilton14"} Gelca-Hamilton 14
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Gelca14"} Gelca 14
          %p
            Since from the point of view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            this is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavefunction"} wavefunction
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi z
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi(\mathbf{z},\mathbf{\tau})
          %p
            For nonabelian CS/WZW theory the same story goes through and one may call the elements of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            “generalized theta functions” (
            %a{:href => "#BeauvilleLaszlo93"}> Beauville-Laszlo 93
            ).
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            Consider a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+torus"} complex torus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \simeq V/\Gamma
            for given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
          %p
            Say that a
            %em system of multipliers
            is a system of invertible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+functions"} holomorphic functions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi γ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo ×
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  e_\gamma \colon V \longrightarrow \mathbb{C}^\times \hookrightarrow \mathbb{C}
          %p satisfying the cocycle condition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mi γ
                      %mo +
                      %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo +
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  e_{\gamma + \delta}(z) = e_\gamma(z + \delta) e_\delta(z)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Then a
            %em theta function
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+function"} holomorphic function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\theta \colon V \longrightarrow \mathbb{C}
          %p
            for which there is a system of multipliers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e_\gamma\}
            satisfying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+equation"} functional equation
            which says that for each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z \in V
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma \in \Gamma \hookrightarrow V
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo +
                  %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\theta(z + \gamma) = e_\gamma(z) \theta(z)
                  \\,.
          %p
            e.g. (
            %a{:href => "#Beauville"}> Beauville, above prop. 2.2
            ), also (
            %a{:href => "#Beauville"}> Beauville, section 3.4
            )
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+theta+function"} Jacobi theta function
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+theta+function"} Riemann theta function
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Ramanujan theta function
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Ramanujan+theta+function"} ?
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+eta+function"} Dedekind eta function
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verlinde+formula"} Verlinde formula
                computes the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
                of spaces of non-abelian theta functions
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+functions"} special functions
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+structure+on+a+line+bundle"} cubical structure on a line bundle
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord
                  mock theta function
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/mock+theta+function"} ?
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+function"} elliptic function
          %div
            %p
              The following table lists classes of examples of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+roots"} square roots
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundles"} line bundles
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th line bundle
                  %th square root
                  %th choice corresponds to
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+bundle"} canonical bundle
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theta+characteristic"} Theta characteristic
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    over
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
                    and
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+manifold"} Hermitian manifold
                    (e.g.
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+manifold"}> Kähler manifold
                    ):
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density+bundle"} density bundle
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/half-density+bundle"} half-density bundle
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+bundle"} canonical bundle
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+submanifold"} Lagrangian submanifold
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metalinear+structure"} metalinear structure
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metaplectic+correction"} metaplectic correction
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant+line+bundle"} determinant line bundle
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pfaffian+line+bundle"} Pfaffian line bundle
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    quadratic
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/secondary+intersection+pairing"} secondary intersection pairing
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual higher gauge theory
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+Wu+structure"} integral Wu structure
          %h2#references References
          %p Introductions to the traditional notion include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                D.H. Bailey et al,
                %em The Miracle of Theta Functions
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.cecm.sfu.ca/organics/papers/borwein/paper/html/node12.html"}> web
                )
            %li
              %p
                M. Bertola,
                %em Riemann surfaces and theta functions
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.mathstat.concordia.ca/faculty/bertola/ThetaCourse/ThetaCourse.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p Modern textbook accounts include
          %ul
            %li#Mumford83
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Mumford"}> David Mumford
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Tata Lectures on Theta
            %li#Polishchuk03
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Polishchuk"}> Alexander Polishchuk
                , section 17 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Abelian varieties, Theta functions and the Fourier transform
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math1.unice.fr/~beauvill/pubs/poli.pdf"} review pdf
          %p
            Further discussion with an emphasis of the origin of theta functions in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Beauville
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arnaud+Beauville"}> Arnaud Beauville
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Theta functions, old and new
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.unice.fr/~beauvill/pubs/thetaon.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Tyurin02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrei+Tyurin"}> Andrei Tyurin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantization, Classical and quantum field theory and theta functions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0210466"} arXiv:math/0210466v1
            %li#Nohara
              %p
                Yuichi Nohara,
                %em Independence of polarization in geometric quantization
                (
                %a{:href => "http://geoquant.mi.ras.ru/nohara.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                Gerard Lion,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michele+Vergne"} Michele Vergne
                %em The Weil representation, Maslov index and theta series
          %p
            Specifically the theta functions appearing in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            and as spaces of sections of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundles"} prequantum line bundles
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+Chern-Simons+theory"} quantization of Chern-Simons theory
            are discussed for instance in
          %ul
            %li#AlvaresGaumeMooreVafa86
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luis+Alvarez-Gaum%C3%A9"}> Luis Alvarez-Gaumé
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"} Gregory Moore
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Theta functions, modular invariance, and strings
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104115581"} Euclid
            %li#AlvaresGaumeBostMooreNelsonVafa87
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luis+Alvarez-Gaum%C3%A9"}> Luis Alvarez-Gaumé
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Benoit+Bost"} Jean-Benoit Bost
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"} Gregory Moore
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Bosonization on higher genus Riemann surfaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104159982"} Euclid
            %li#Freed87
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                , around p. 30-31 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On determinant line bundles
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.utexas.edu/~dafr/Index/determinants.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/dg-ga/9505002"} dg-ga/9505002
            %li#FalcetoGawedzki94
              %p
                Fernando Falceto,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gaw%C4%99dzki"} Krzysztof Gawędzki
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Chern-Simons states at genus one
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104254732"} Euclid
            %li
              %p
                Kazuhiro Hikami,
                %em Mock (False) Theta Functions as Quantum Invariants
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0506073"}> arXiv:math-ph/0506073
                )
            %li
              %p
                Kazuhiro Hikami,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Invariants, Modular Forms, and Lattice Points II
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0604091"} arXiv:math/0604091
            %li#GelcaUribe10a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Razvan+Gelca"}> Razvan Gelca
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alejandro+Uribe"} Alejandro Uribe
                %em From classical theta functions to topological quantum field theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1006.3252"}> arXiv:1006.3252
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.ttu.edu/~rgelca/berk.pdf"} slides pdf
            %li#GelcaUribe10b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Razvan+Gelca"}> Razvan Gelca
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alejandro+Uribe"} Alejandro Uribe
                %em
                  Quantum mechanics and non-abelian theta functions for the gauge group
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1007.2010"}> arXiv:1007.2010
                )
            %li#GelcaHamilton12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Razvan+Gelca"}> Razvan Gelca
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alastair+Hamilton"} Alastair Hamilton
                %em Classical theta functions from a quantum group perspective
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1209.1135"}> arXiv:1209.1135
                )
            %li#GelcaHamilton14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Razvan+Gelca"}> Razvan Gelca
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alastair+Hamilton"} Alastair Hamilton
                %em The topological quantum field theory of Riemann’s theta functions
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1406.4269"}> arXiv:1406.4269
                )
            %li#Gelca14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Razvan+Gelca"}> Razvan Gelca
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Theta Functions and Knots
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.worldscientific.com/doi/suppl/10.1142/8872/suppl_file/8872_chap01.pdf"} prologue pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.worldscientific.com/worldscibooks/10.1142/8872"} publisher page
            %li#Andersen11
              %p
                Johan Martens
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%B8rgen+Andersen"} Jørgen Andersen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological quantum field theories and moduli spaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://maths.fuglede.dk/noter/tqftms.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and more generally the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+functions"} partition functions
            of connection-twisted Dirac operators on even-dimensional locally symmetric spaces is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#BunkeOlbrich94
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Olbrich"} Martin Olbrich
              %em Theta and zeta functions for locally symmetric spaces of rank one
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/dg-ga/9407013"}> arXiv:dg-ga/9407013
              )
          %p
            Generalization of this from abelian to non-abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            to “generalized theta functions” appears in
          %ul
            %li#BeauvilleLaszlo93
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arnaud+Beauville"}> Arnaud Beauville
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yves+Laszlo"} Yves Laszlo
              = succeed "," do
                %em Conformal blocks and generalized theta functions
              %strong 164
              (1994), 385 - 419,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104270837"} euclid
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/alg-geom/9309003"} alg-geom/9309003
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=1289330"} MR1289330
          %p brief review is in
          %ul
            %li#Gawedzki99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gawedzki"}> Krzysztof Gawedzki
              , section 5 of
              %em Conformal field theory: a case study
              in Y. Nutku, C. Saclioglu, T. Turgut (eds.)
              %em Frontier in Physics
              102, Perseus Publishing (2000) (
              %a{:href => "http://xxx.lanl.gov/abs/hep-th/9904145"}> hep-th/9904145
              )
          %p
            That the Riemann zeta functions are the local coordinate expressions of the covariantly constant sections of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hitchin+connection"} Hitchin connection
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#Hitchin90
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nigel+Hitchin"}> Nigel Hitchin
              , remark 4.12 in
              = succeed "," do
                %em Flat connections and geometric quantization
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104200841"} Euclid
          %p
            Relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genera"} elliptic genera
            (see also at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+form"} Jacobi form
          %ul
            %li#KL95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kefeng+Liu"}> Kefeng Liu
              , section 2.4 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em On modular invariance and rigidity theorems
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214456221"} EUCLID
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.ucla.edu/~liu/Research/loja.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Theta functions for higher dimensional varieties and their relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphic+forms"} automorphic forms
            is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Weil"}> André Weil
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Sur certaines groups d’operateur unitaires
          %p
            see
            %a{:href => "Langlands+program#Gelbhart84"} Gelbhart 84, page 35 (211)
            for review.
          %p Further developments here include
          %ul
            %li#Kudla77
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Kudla"}> Stephen Kudla
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Relations between automorphic forms produced by theta-functions
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Modular Functions of One Variable VI
            %li#Kudla78
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Kudla"}> Stephen Kudla
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Theta functions and Hilbert modular forms
            %li#Stopple95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeffrey+Stopple"}> Jeffrey Stopple
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Theta and
                    = succeed "-function" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi L
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://matwbn.icm.edu.pl/ksiazki/aa/aa72/aa7221.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Yum-Tong Siu,
                %em Theta functions in higher dimensions
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/SiuHigherTheta.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                )
        .revisedby
